// Champion decisions. main.cpp dispatches here after the draft.
//
// Bamboo7: Bamboo6 adopting the ladder leaders' habits (Mite, KratosMessi).
//
// Bamboo5 strategy (Bamboo4 that stays inside its fuel budget):
//   solo    — while no enemies are in sight, champions split up and each farms
//             camps it can clear alone (monsters included), spread across the
//             map. Targets are scored by path distance once each camp's path
//             field is cached.
//   fuel    — a turn that runs out of fuel resumes next turn, losing actions:
//             avoid vision::camps() (quadratic in camps), cache engine data.
//   squads  — once enemies show up, the team regroups in pairs (an odd champion
//             makes one trio; Cassi and Issac always pair up). The first alive
//             slot of a squad leads: it picks the squad's camp group and the
//             others follow. Monsters are only engaged once the party has
//             gathered.
//   capture — stand on a spawn tile of a cleared group until its reward lands.
//   guard   — after a capture, stay near central or recently contested groups
//             (off the spawn tiles) when they respawn soon, with a ward for warning.
//   alerts  — shared memory carries one team alert: defend a group under attack,
//             avoid a group where we just lost a fight (farm elsewhere and come
//             back stronger), or contest an altar an enemy is banking at.
//   vision  — each champion keeps a ward on its assigned spot: bushes near the
//             map centre or near altars, falling back to gaps between walls.
//   altars  — carry an altar lock and drop it on unlocked altars we pass; it
//             blocks only enemy tributes.
//   tribute — carry gems to the nearest altar at a threshold (lower when an
//             altar is a few steps away), near the round limit, or when the
//             team is about to win.
//   recover — at low health walk out of danger and recall; heal on spawn and
//             spend gold on emblems there (or while dead).
//   fight   — enemy champions in attack range take priority over camps, but only
//             when the local strength (health x damage of each side) favours
//             us; otherwise we back off, stunning or hitting chasers on the
//             way. Never chase far.
